      "writtenOn": "2026-08-21T07:00:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Was answered in meeting, summarizing here just to keep it \"on paper\")\nBecause we need to replace the uutils coreutils with the original GNU coreutils, and coreutils are essential packages, manipulating or replacing one coreutils with another requires `--allow-remove-essential`.\nHere it is safe because we are removing one coreutils base and installing another coreutils base, if we were just removing coreutils **without** installing a different coreutils, it would be a dangerous operation (which is why it requires a dedicated \"I am aware this can break my system\" flag)\n\nWe need the original GNU coreutils because the uutils coreutils (sudo especially) don\u0027t work in evssim infrastructure, some things just break and CI fails.",
      "parentUuid": "fb438241_6d57e9c7",
      "range": {
